{
  "_readme": [
    "Register lexicon: formal legal Bangla (and the English of the un-replaced colonial Acts) mapped to how citizens actually say the same thing.",
    "Two jobs. (1) Tier-B synthetic question generation rewrites a provision title through this map so the generated question does not simply echo the statute. (2) Topic 4 (seq2seq colloquial->formal register translation) trains on it as a seed dictionary alongside the PAIR annotations.",
    "Hand-authored, not mined. Entries are the ones that actually separate the two registers in this corpus - a term belongs here only if a citizen would plausibly never use the legal form. Neutral vocabulary is deliberately absent.",
    "Direction of the map is legal -> citizen, because that is the direction generation needs. Topic 4 inverts it."
  ],
